    <bpmn:process id="W_W4B" name="W4B. Store-Initiated Replenishment Request" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store Manager or Department Supervisor identifies local demand that exceeds current replenishment plan (e.g., nearby construction project, local event, weather-driven spike)
Frequency: ~100–200 store-initiated requests/month chain-wide; ~0.5–1 per store per month
Volume: Typically 5–20 SKUs per request
Owner: Supply Planner
Participants: Store Manager / Dept. Supervisor, Supply Planner, Buyer (if new PO needed)
Source: workflow W4B — Store-Initiated Replenishment Request</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4B_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4B_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4B_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4B_Lane3" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4B_Lane4" name="Per W4">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4B_Lane5" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4B_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4B_Start7" name="Store Manager or Department Supervisor identifies local demand that exceeds current…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task8" name="Store Manager or Dept. Supervisor identifies items needing additional stock…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Store Manager or Dept. Supervisor identifies items needing additional stock beyond automated replenishment; opens replenishment request in system (handheld or terminal) — selects SKUs, enters requested quantity, urgency (routine / expedited / emergency), and business justification (e.g., &quot;new subdivision project starting 2 km away&quot;)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Dept. Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W4B_Task9" name="System checks: (a) current on-hand at store, (b) current on-hand at serving DC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System checks: (a) current on-hand at store, (b) current on-hand at serving DC, (c) open POs and incoming replenishment orders, (d) ATP at DC after existing commitments; presents Supply Planner with a dashboard showing the request alongside existing supply position
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task10" name="Supply Planner reviews request each morning alongside standard replenishment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supply Planner reviews request each morning alongside standard replenishment review (W4 step 2); evaluates: (a) is the demand legitimate and near-term, (b) does DC have available stock to fulfill without depriving other stores, (c) if expedited — can it ride on the next wave, or does it need a separate shipment
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task11" name="If approved — DC has stock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If approved — DC has stock: Supply Planner adds requested quantities to the next replenishment order for that store (W4 step 2); system creates a pick task in the next wave; request status updated to &quot;Approved — Scheduled&quot;
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task12" name="If approved — DC has insufficient stock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If approved — DC has insufficient stock: Supply Planner requests Buyer to expedite a PO (W2A) or arrange an inter-DC transfer (W22); request status updated to &quot;Approved — Pending Supply&quot;; Supply Planner tracks until supply arrives
Responsible (R): Supply Planner / Buyer
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task13" name="If denied">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: If denied: Supply Planner rejects request with reason (insufficient DC stock, lower priority than other stores, demand not validated); system notifies Store Manager; Store Manager may escalate to Regional Manager if disagreement
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task14" name="Fulfillment follows standard W4 pick/pack/ship process; request closed when…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Fulfillment follows standard W4 pick/pack/ship process; request closed when goods received at store
Responsible (R): Per W4
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W4</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4B_Task15" name="Weekly: Supply Planning Manager reviews store-initiated request report —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: Supply Planning Manager reviews store-initiated request report — approval rate, top requesting stores, frequently requested items; flags items with high ad-hoc request frequency for ROP/safety stock adjustment per W31.8
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4B_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4B_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4B_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4B_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: (none recorded)
Owner: Supply Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
