    <bpmn:process id="W_W56" name="W56. Customer Backorder Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests an item that is out of stock at the store and/or DC level
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 backorder requests/month (primarily B2B trade accounts)
Volume: Concentrated in fast-moving commodity categories (cement, lumber, paint, plumbing fittings, electrical wire) during peak construction season
Owner: Sales Associate (intake); Supply Planner (fulfillment)
Participants: Sales Associate, Supply Planner, Buyer, Store Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W56 — Customer Backorder Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W56_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W56_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W56_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W56_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W56_Lane4" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W56_Lane5" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_Task20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W56_End21</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W56_Start7" name="Customer requests an item that is out of stock at the store and/or DC level">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task8" name="Customer requests out-of-stock item at store or via Sales Rep; Sales Associate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer requests out-of-stock item at store or via Sales Rep; Sales Associate checks real-time inventory across all locations (stores + DCs) via handheld
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Dept. Supervisor
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task9" name="If available at another store: offer customer-initiated inter-store transfer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: If available at another store: offer customer-initiated inter-store transfer per W22 (customer-initiated transfer)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task10" name="If unavailable chain-wide or customer prefers to wait: Sales Associate creates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If unavailable chain-wide or customer prefers to wait: Sales Associate creates backorder in system — item, quantity, customer details (loyalty account or trade account), preferred store for pickup, delivery preference, maximum wait time (customer-stated)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Dept. Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task11" name="System links backorder to next expected replenishment: (a) if PO already in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System links backorder to next expected replenishment: (a) if PO already in progress (W2) with expected GR date — system shows estimated availability date, (b) if no PO exists — system flags to Supply Planner for PO creation (W2A), (c) if import item — shows import PO ETA (W2B)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task12" name="System reserves backorder quantity against incoming PO or replenishment order…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System reserves backorder quantity against incoming PO or replenishment order (allocates to backorder before general store replenishment); backorder takes priority over routine replenishment allocation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task13" name="Sales Associate communicates estimated availability date to customer; for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Sales Associate communicates estimated availability date to customer; for trade/corporate accounts, Sales Rep manages the communication
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Sales Rep
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task14" name="When goods are received at DC and backorder allocation is fulfilled: system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: When goods are received at DC and backorder allocation is fulfilled: system routes allocated quantity to the customer&#x27;s preferred store in the next replenishment wave (W4); or if customer prefers delivery, system creates home delivery order (W19)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Supply Planner
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task15" name="System sends customer notification (SMS/email/app): &quot;Your item is on the way to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: System sends customer notification (SMS/email/app): &quot;Your item is on the way to [Store Name], expected availability [date]&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task16" name="Item arrives at store; Stock Associate stages for customer pickup (similar to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Item arrives at store; Stock Associate stages for customer pickup (similar to BOPIS W11); system sends &quot;Ready for pickup&quot; notification
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min + automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task17" name="Customer picks up item; sale processed at POS (standard transaction or trade…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Customer picks up item; sale processed at POS (standard transaction or trade account per W5B.4c); backorder closed in system
Responsible (R): Cashier / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task18" name="If customer cancels backorder before fulfillment: Sales Associate cancels in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: If customer cancels backorder before fulfillment: Sales Associate cancels in system; allocation released back to general inventory
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Dept. Supervisor
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W56_Task19" name="If backorder exceeds customer-stated maximum wait time: system auto-notifies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: If backorder exceeds customer-stated maximum wait time: system auto-notifies customer with options to (a) extend wait, (b) accept substitute item, or (c) cancel; if no response in 7 days, system auto-cancels and releases allocation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W56_Task20" name="Weekly: Supply Planner reviews open backorder aging report: items with no…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 13: Weekly: Supply Planner reviews open backorder aging report: items with no incoming PO (step 4b — no supply planned), long-wait backorders (&gt; 14 days), and backorders at risk of cancellation; escalates to Buyer for expedited procurement
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W56_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W56_End21" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W56_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W56_Annotation22">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-253 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Accuracy &amp; Counting (PA-05.1).) | - operational: Sales Associate (intake); Supply Planner (fulfillment) review and approval gate
Owner: Sales Associate (intake); Supply Planner (fulfillment)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
