    <bpmn:process id="W_W514" name="W514. Inventory Count Reconciliation &amp; Variance Root Cause Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cycle count (W6) or physical inventory (W42) completion reveals variance exceeding configurable thresholds
Frequency: Weekly per store (from daily cycle counts); annually from wall-to-wall physical inventory
Volume: ~200–300 variance investigations/month across 200 stores; ~50–80 requiring full root cause analysis
Owner: Inventory Control Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Stock Associate, Inventory Analyst, Loss Prevention Officer
Source: workflow W514 — Inventory Count Reconciliation &amp; Variance Root Cause Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W514_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W514_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W514_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W514_Lane3" name="Inventory Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W514_Lane4" name="Inventory Control Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W514_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W514_Start6" name="Cycle count (W6) or physical inventory (W42) completion reveals variance exceeding…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W514_Task7" name="System flags variances from completed counts against configurable thresholds…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System flags variances from completed counts against configurable thresholds: A-items &gt;±0.5% or &gt;±PHP 5K; B-items &gt;±1% or &gt;±PHP 3K; C-items &gt;±2% or &gt;±PHP 1K; generates variance exception report per store
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task8" name="Store Manager reviews variance exception report for their store; performs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager reviews variance exception report for their store; performs initial assessment: (a) obvious data entry error (transposed digits, wrong SKU scanned) → immediate correction with documentation; (b) legitimate unexplained variance → route to Inventory Analyst
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Inventory Control Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task9" name="For unexplained variances: Inventory Analyst opens variance investigation case…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For unexplained variances: Inventory Analyst opens variance investigation case; system auto-populates: SKU details, count vs. system quantity, dollar value of variance, last 3 count results for this SKU, recent transaction history (receipts, transfers, sales, adjustments)
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): Inventory Control Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task10" name="Inventory Analyst categorizes suspected root cause: (a) Receiving error…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inventory Analyst categorizes suspected root cause: (a) Receiving error (quantity mismatch at GR); (b) Miscount (counter error, counted wrong SKU); (c) Unit-of-measure confusion (case vs. piece); (d) System error (integration failure, duplicate posting); (e) Unpicked/unstorable inventory in wrong location; (f) Shrinkage/theft (no other explanation)
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): Inventory Control Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task11" name="For receiving errors: Inventory Analyst traces to original GR document…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For receiving errors: Inventory Analyst traces to original GR document; contacts DC or vendor to verify shipment quantity; if confirmed short shipment, initiates vendor claim (W88) or DC discrepancy resolution
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): Inventory Control Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task12" name="For suspected shrinkage/theft (variance &gt;PHP 10K or pattern across multiple…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For suspected shrinkage/theft (variance &gt;PHP 10K or pattern across multiple counts): Inventory Analyst escalates to Loss Prevention Officer for investigation (W248); LP Officer reviews CCTV, EBR exceptions, and employee access logs
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task13" name="Inventory Analyst documents root cause finding and recommended corrective…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Inventory Analyst documents root cause finding and recommended corrective action in variance case: (a) process improvement (receiving checklist, count procedure update); (b) system fix (integration correction, master data update); (c) LP referral; (d) no action (within acceptable tolerance)
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): Inventory Control Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task14" name="Inventory Control Manager reviews and closes variance case; approves corrective…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Inventory Control Manager reviews and closes variance case; approves corrective action; system updates inventory with approved adjustment (W92) referencing variance case number
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task15" name="Monthly: Inventory Control Manager generates variance root cause dashboard…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly: Inventory Control Manager generates variance root cause dashboard: variance rate by store, category, and root cause; top 20 stores by variance rate; top 20 SKUs by recurrence; corrective action completion rate
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W514_Task16" name="Quarterly: Inventory Control Manager presents variance trend analysis to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Quarterly: Inventory Control Manager presents variance trend analysis to operations leadership: variance rate trend (goal: &lt;1.5% shrinkage), root cause distribution, most improved/declined stores, systemic issues requiring capital investment (e.g., CCTV upgrades, receiving process redesign)
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W514_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W514_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W514_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W514_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-253 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Accuracy &amp; Counting (PA-05.1).) | - operational: mandatory investigation documentation for variances &gt;PHP 5K and quarterly unknown-rate target (&lt;15%); operational: tiered approach (A-items prioritized, C-items batch-processed monthly)
Owner: Inventory Control Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W514_Assoc19" sourceRef="W514_Annotation18" targetRef="W514_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W514_Flow20" sourceRef="W514_Start6" targetRef="W514_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W514_Flow21" sourceRef="W514_Task7" targetRef="W514_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W514_Flow22" sourceRef="W514_Task8" targetRef="W514_Task9" />
