    <bpmn:process id="W_W1275" name="W1275. Store-Level Daily Consignment Inventory Sales Reconciliation &amp; Vendor Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store closing reconciliation; consignment sell-through data accumulation
Frequency: Daily per store; consolidated vendor reports generated weekly and monthly
Volume: ~300 consignment SKUs across 200 stores from ~12 key vendors; ~5,000–8,000 consignment units sold daily chain-wide
Owner: Cash Office Clerk (store-level); Merchandise Admin (HQ vendor reporting)
Participants: Cash Office Clerk, Store Manager, Merchandise Admin, AP Clerk (vendor settlement), Category Manager
Source: workflow W1275 — Store-Level Daily Consignment Inventory Sales Reconciliation &amp; Vendor Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1275_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1275_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1275_Lane2" name="Cash Office Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1275_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1275_Lane4" name="Merchandise Admin">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1275_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1275_Start6" name="Daily store closing reconciliation; consignment sell-through data accumulation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1275_Task7" name="End-of-day consignment report generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: End-of-day consignment report generation: at store closing per W574, system generates daily consignment sales report: (a) list of all consignment items sold today at this store: SKU, description, quantity, unit price, total amount, transaction reference, (b) summary by vendor: vendor name, total units sold, total sales value, (c) any consignment returns processed today (reversals), (d) current consignment on-hand balance per SKU (system)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1275_Task8" name="Cash Office Clerk verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cash Office Clerk verification: Cash Office Clerk reviews consignment report as part of daily cash office routine (W541): (a) verifies consignment sales total on report matches POS consignment tender/sales totals from Z-report, (b) flags any line items with quantity &gt; 5 units of a single consignment SKU in one day (unusual; may indicate error or theft), (c) checks for consignment returns &gt; 2 units (may indicate quality issue or return fraud), (d) if discrepancies found between consignment report and POS totals: escalates to Store Manager
Responsible (R): Cash Office Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1275_Task9" name="Consignment shrinkage check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consignment shrinkage check: Store Manager or Department Supervisor performs daily visual check of high-value consignment items (major appliances, premium tiles): (a) physical count of display units in appliance section and tile gallery for top 20 consignment SKUs by value, (b) compare physical count to system on-hand balance, (c) if physical count &lt; system count (missing item): (i) check if item was sold but POS not processed (system error), (ii) check CCTV for the specific SKU location, (iii) if confirmed shrinkage: log as consignment loss — BuildRight liable to vendor at consignment cost price; report per W562 (loss prevention daily routine), (d) if physical count &gt; system count (extra item): verify receiving — may be unreceived vendor replenishment
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1275_Task10" name="Daily data confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Daily data confirmation: Cash Office Clerk confirms daily consignment reconciliation in system: (a) confirms consignment report verified — no discrepancies, or documents discrepancies with resolution notes, (b) system publishes daily consignment sell-through data to vendor settlement accumulation table (used by W1188/W1230 for monthly settlement), (c) data flagged as &quot;reconciled&quot; or &quot;has exception&quot;
Responsible (R): Cash Office Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1275_Task11" name="Weekly vendor consignment report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly vendor consignment report: Merchandise Admin generates weekly consignment sell-through report per vendor: (a) total units sold by SKU across all 200 stores, (b) total sales value and consignment cost value, (c) store-level detail for any stores flagged with exceptions, (d) inventory balance by SKU by store vs. vendor-provided replenishment quantities, (e) report shared with Category Manager and vendor via vendor portal (W705)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Admin
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1275_Task12" name="Monthly vendor reconciliation preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly vendor reconciliation preparation: Merchandise Admin prepares month-end consignment data for vendor settlement per W1188/W1230: (a) aggregate daily reconciled data into monthly summary per vendor per SKU, (b) include: units sold, sales value, consignment cost, BuildRight shrinkage liability (step 3), any pending disputes, (c) generate vendor settlement statement for AP processing per W1230
Responsible (R): Merchandise Admin
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1275_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1275_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1275_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1275_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-253 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Accuracy &amp; Counting (PA-05.1).) | - operational: on-hand is understated, creating apparent shrinkage
Owner: Cash Office Clerk (store-level); Merchandise Admin (HQ vendor reporting)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
