    <bpmn:process id="W_W1413" name="W1413. DC-Level Cycle Count Discrepancy Root Cause Analysis, Corrective Action &amp; Recount Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cycle count variance exceeds threshold (&gt; 1% by value or &gt; 3 units per SKU); or recurring variance on same SKU/location across consecutive counts
Frequency: Triggered — approximately 5–10% of daily cycle counts produce actionable variances at 4 DCs; ~80–100 discrepancy investigations/month (per the Time Estimate ≈25/DC/month)
Volume: ~1,000–1,200 DC cycle count discrepancy investigations/year (≈100/month per the Time Estimate); recurring discrepancy patterns affect ~50–100 SKU-locations
Owner: DC Operations Manager
Participants: DC Operations Manager, Inventory Control Clerk, Warehouse Supervisor, LP Officer, Supply Planner
Source: workflow W1413 — DC-Level Cycle Count Discrepancy Root Cause Analysis, Corrective Action &amp; Recount Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1413_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1413_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1413_Lane2" name="Inventory Control Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1413_Lane3" name="DC Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1413_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1413_Start5" name="Cycle count variance exceeds threshold (&gt; 1% by value or &gt; 3 units per SKU); or recurring…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1413_Task6" name="Cycle count completes (W6); system compares physical count to system on-hand…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Cycle count completes (W6); system compares physical count to system on-hand; if variance exceeds threshold: (a) value variance &gt; 1% of SKU value at that location, or (b) quantity variance &gt; 3 units, or (c) SKU has been flagged as &quot;recurring variance&quot; in previous 3 counts: system automatically flags count for investigation and holds the adjustment from posting
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task7" name="Inventory Control Clerk receives investigation alert with details: SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inventory Control Clerk receives investigation alert with details: SKU, location (bin/slot), system on-hand, physical count, variance (units and value), SKU velocity (A/B/C), and count history (number of variances on this SKU/location in last 12 months)
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Clerk
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task8" name="Immediate recount">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Immediate recount: Inventory Control Clerk performs blind recount of the flagged SKU at the flagged location (does not see expected count); if recount matches original physical count: variance confirmed; if recount matches system on-hand: original count was in error, variance cleared, no further investigation needed
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Clerk
Accountable (A): Warehouse Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task9" name="If variance confirmed after recount: Inventory Control Clerk expands search to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If variance confirmed after recount: Inventory Control Clerk expands search to adjacent locations (same SKU may be in multiple bins): (a) check reserve storage locations for the SKU, (b) check staging areas for pending outbound shipments, (c) check dock area for recently received but not-yet-putaway inventory; if missing quantity is found in an alternate location: location error identified, bin-to-bin transfer posted, root cause = &quot;Putaway Location Error&quot;
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Clerk
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task10" name="If missing quantity not found in alternate locations: Inventory Control Clerk…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If missing quantity not found in alternate locations: Inventory Control Clerk checks transaction history for the SKU at that location for the past 7 days: (a) all inbound receipts (W3), (b) all outbound picks (W4, W22), (c) any bin-to-bin transfers, (d) any returns processing (W651), (e) any adjustments posted; looks for unconfirmed picks (picked but not shipped), uncompleted putaways (received but not confirmed to bin), or quantity entry errors
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task11" name="Receiving Error">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Inventory Control Clerk classifies root cause from standardized dropdown: (a) Receiving Error — GR quantity incorrect vs. actual received; (b) Putaway Error — items put to wrong bin/location; (c) Pick Error — wrong quantity picked for outbound order; (d) Shipping Error — quantity shipped differs from pick quantity; (e) Damaged/Destroyed — items damaged and removed but not recorded; (f) Theft/Shrinkage — no operational explanation found; escalate to LP; (g) System Error — software processing error (rare); (h) Documentation Error — transaction entered incorrectly
Responsible (R): Inventory Control Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task12" name="Corrective action by root cause">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Corrective action by root cause: (a) Receiving Error — retrain Receiving Clerk on count verification, add dual-count protocol for high-value items; (b) Putaway Error — verify WMS directed putaway accuracy, retrain putaway staff; (c) Pick Error — check pick path accuracy, verify RF scanner calibration, retrain picker; (d) Shipping Error — add pack verification scan before dispatch; (e) Damaged — update damage reporting process, add damage chute signage; (f) Theft — escalate to LP Officer for investigation per W37, review CCTV, check employee access logs; (g) System Error — report to IT Helpdesk (W48) for investigation; (h) Documentation Error — retrain on transaction entry
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager / Warehouse Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task13" name="DC Operations Manager approves inventory adjustment: system posts adjustment to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: DC Operations Manager approves inventory adjustment: system posts adjustment to correct on-hand; adjustment journal entry created with root cause code, investigation notes, and corrective action reference; GL impact: Dr/Cr Inventory with offset to Shrinkage/Damage/Loss account per chart of accounts
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): Controller (if value &gt; PHP 50,000)
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task14" name="Recurring variance escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Recurring variance escalation: if same SKU/location has 3+ variances in 12 months: system flags as chronic; DC Operations Manager initiates deep investigation: (a) 30-day intensive monitoring with daily micro-counts of the SKU/location, (b) process observation — DC Operations Manager physically observes receiving, putaway, and picking activities for the SKU, (c) bin location physical audit — verify bin dimensions and capacity match WMS configuration, (d) if theft suspected: LP Officer installs targeted CCTV or conducts covert surveillance per W23
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager / LP Officer
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1413_Task15" name="Monthly: DC Operations Manager generates cycle count discrepancy analysis…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly: DC Operations Manager generates cycle count discrepancy analysis report: (a) total variances by root cause category, (b) total inventory value adjustment, (c) top 20 SKU-locations by recurring variance frequency, (d) corrective action closure rate, (e) DC inventory accuracy trend (target ≥ 99% for A-items, ≥ 97% overall); report shared with VP Supply Chain and Controller
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1413_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1413_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1413_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1413_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-253 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Accuracy &amp; Counting (PA-05.1).) | - operational: DC Operations Manager review and approval gate
Owner: DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1413_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1413_Annotation17" targetRef="W1413_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1413_Flow19" sourceRef="W1413_Start5" targetRef="W1413_Task6" />
