    <bpmn:process id="W_W1486" name="W1486. Lumber Yard Inventory Measurement, Board Foot Calculation &amp; Dimensional Grading Verification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly cycle count schedule for lumber yard; also triggered upon receipt of lumber shipments and when discrepancy between system quantity and physical count exceeds 3%
Frequency: Weekly cycle count; per-shipment verification on receipt; monthly full yard reconciliation
Volume: ~50–80 SKUs per store in lumber/builder&#x27;s wood; ~15–30 lumber receipts/store/month; weekly spot-check of 10–15 SKUs
Owner: Lumber Yard Supervisor
Participants: Lumber Yard Associate, Stock Associate, Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1486 — Lumber Yard Inventory Measurement, Board Foot Calculation &amp; Dimensional Grading Verification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1486_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1486_Lane1" name="Lumber Yard Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1486_Lane2" name="Lumber Yard Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1486_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1486_Start4" name="Weekly cycle count schedule for lumber yard; also triggered upon receipt of lumber…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1486_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1486_Task5" name="Lumber receipt dimensional verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lumber receipt dimensional verification: When lumber shipment arrives: (a) Lumber Yard Associate counts bundles per delivery receipt; (b) for each species/size, associate measures a sample of 5 pieces from different bundles using tape measure; (c) actual dimensions recorded and board foot calculated per piece; (d) average bf per piece × piece count × bundles = received bf; (e) variance &gt; 5% from supplier invoice triggers dispute per PA-15.1; (f) moisture meter reading taken from 3 random pieces per species; (g) if moisture &gt; 20% for kiln-dried lumber: shipment may be rejected or accepted at discount
Responsible (R): Lumber Yard Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber Yard Supervisor
Duration: 30–45 min per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1486_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1486_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1486_Task6" name="Weekly lumber yard cycle count">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly lumber yard cycle count: Weekly: (a) system selects 10–15 lumber SKUs for spot count based on ABC classification and time since last count; (b) Lumber Yard Associate physically counts pieces per SKU in the yard; (c) for high-value species (yakal, apitong), associate verifies dimensions of 3 random pieces per bundle to confirm grading; (d) system compares physical count to book quantity; (e) variance &gt; 3% triggers recount and root cause investigation; (f) adjustment posted per PA-05.1 cycle count adjustment workflow with supervisor approval required for adjustments &gt; PHP 10,000
Responsible (R): Lumber Yard Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber Yard Supervisor
Duration: 60–90 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1486_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1486_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1486_Task7" name="Bundle integrity monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Bundle integrity monitoring: Daily: (a) Lumber Yard Associate walks the yard checking bundle bands/strapping; (b) opened or partially depleted bundles re-tallied; (c) loose pieces identified and returned to correct bundles or written off as damaged; (d) customer-rejected pieces (warped, split, knotty beyond grade) set aside for markdown per PA-05.3 disposition rules; (e) findings logged in system for shrinkage tracking
Responsible (R): Lumber Yard Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1486_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1486_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1486_Task8" name="Monthly board foot reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly board foot reconciliation: Monthly: (a) system generates lumber inventory valuation report showing book bf vs. theoretical bf based on receipts minus sales; (b) Lumber Yard Supervisor reconciles with physical yard inventory; (c) dimensional shrinkage factor applied (Philippine lumber typically shrinks 2–5% from green to air-dry state); (d) unexplained loss &gt; 2% of monthly lumber COGS escalated to LP team per PA-23.3; (e) findings feed into vendor performance scorecard for lumber suppliers
Responsible (R): Lumber Yard Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1486_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1486_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1486_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1486_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1486_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-253 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Accuracy &amp; Counting (PA-05.1).) | - operational: must clearly distinguish nominal (for ordering) from actual (for pricing and inventory)
Owner: Lumber Yard Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1486_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1486_Annotation10" targetRef="W1486_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
